From ced3fd64cd1b55634d44284aad01acaf9a810140 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam McLeod <not@telling.github.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 19:29:27 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] HID: hid-steam: 2026 Steam Controller support from Valve
 6.18.42

Valve's hid-steam.c taken verbatim from linux-integration tag
6.18.42-valve2. Adds handling for the 2026 Steam Controller and its
wireless puck: steam_do_ibex_input_event(), steam_do_ibex_sensors_event(),
IIO sensor open/close, rumble coalescing, and the steam_exchange_report()
/ steam_send_report_id() / steam_recv_report_id() transport helpers.

Compiles unmodified against 7.2-rc6 -- no API adjustments were needed.

Not upstream: as of 2026-08-08 neither torvalds/linux nor the HID
maintainer tree carries any of this; the newest hid-steam commits in
both are from the 6.15 era. Drop this patch once Valve post it to
linux-input and it merges.

Without it the puck (28de:1304) falls through to hid-generic and
hid_steam never loads. Steam drives the controller over hidraw either
way, so this is about having a working in-kernel gamepad node.

Origin: Valve Software, linux-integration 6.18.42-valve2 (af6356cf2488)
